= <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>'s Show of Strength

In an attempt to revive the crumbling morale of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, the paramilitary organization staged a provocative march directly in front of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> headquarters—the Verdwen House on Verdwen Square, a major square in one of Axton’s working-class, <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivist**</span>-dominated districts.

Acting under Staal’s orders, Axton police cleared the building “for safety reasons” and protected the route of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> march, deploying armored trucks and machine-gun squads to suppress any hostile fire from the surrounding buildings.

These extreme precautions culminated in the spectacle of fifteen thousand <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> men parading through the square, chanting slogans such as “We shit on freedom! We shit on the <span style="color: #005EB8;">usurper</span> republic!”—with no <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivist**</span> counter-demonstration permitted. When violence broke out, police clashed almost exclusively with <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivist**</span> protestors.

- @nazi_2
- @counter_rally: Answer them in the streets — with the Vanguard beside us.

@nazi_2
title: We are powerless, with the police on their side.
on-arrival: loyalist_strength += 25; loyalist_militancy += 0.02; vanguard_strength += 10; disfavored_collectivist -= 2; disfavored_royalist += 2; commons_collectivist -= 2; commons_royalist += 2; royalist_explode -= 1

In the days that follow, <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> morale experiences a renewed, if temporary, surge. The rally projects an aura of legitimacy, as the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> align themselves with the forces of law and order against the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

For the left, it is a demoralizing blow—an open display of <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> defiance on the very doorstep of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, unopposed and uncontested, with the implicit approval of the government.

@counter_rally
choose-if: collectivist_relation >= 35
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> will not march beside us.
on-arrival: banner_strength += 50; vanguard_strength += 25; commons_marcher += 2; commons_collectivist += 2; loyalist_militancy += 0.02; strife += 1

The square is not left to them. By evening the Banners and the <span style="color: #8B0000;">**Vanguard**</span> fill the far end of it — a counter-column twice shouted down and twice re-formed, under more flags than the two parties have ever flown together. The police keep the columns apart, barely. No one on either side will remember the day as a defeat, which is itself a kind of victory for the republic: the streets, at least, are still contested.